{"actor": "opencode", "data": {"refs": ["tools/originlib/landed.py"], "summary": "Attribution at the end of a session follows a recorded base advance, not git authorship and not another session's artifact list: sync writes a base_advance event naming the commits that arrived, and a landed path whose newest commit is not one of them, or that carries an uncommitted edit, is this session's change again. Git authorship was falsified as a baseline before implementing (both VMs commit as 'Ihsan Ai Server Bot'), and a base move the tooling did not perform deliberately stays reported."}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "decision", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 19, "session": "2026-10-03-042-t-0024-stop-reconciliation-and-the-docum", "ts": "2026-10-04T00:11:22+00:00"}
